      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes how the **Guarded Write Journal** works as a safety mechanism for file operations. Here\u0027s what it covers:\n\n**Core Function:** The write journal records the prior state of any file before the guarded tool executor overwrites it \u2014 capturing either the file\u0027s previous content or noting that it didn\u0027t exist.\n\n**Rollback Capability:** If an agent run fails (due to turn cap exceeded, unrecoverable errors, or denied writes), the journal can roll back all recorded writes in reverse order by:\n- Restoring previous content for files that existed\n- Deleting newly created files\n\n**Transaction Semantics:** This approach provides all-or-nothing semantics for writes without requiring a database transaction \u2014 the in-memory journal itself serves as the transaction log for the duration of a single run.\n\nThe page also notes that the Query agent never uses the journal\u0027s rollback functionality, since the Query agent has no write capability at all.",
